<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Idrieus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 344 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Idrieus was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satrapy">satrap</a> of Caria from 351 to 344 BCE, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hecatomnus">Hecatomnus</a> who succeeded his sister Artemisia II and ruled jointly with his sister and wife Ada. He served the Persian king loyally, sending Carian forces to help recover <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a> from rebels. On his death Ada ruled alone.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/idrieus.jpg" alt="Idrieus" width="320" height="165" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SATRAPS_of_CARIA._Hidrieus._Circa_351-0_to_344-3_BC.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
